Surface CompileError from Structure::close

TypeConflict is gone. close() takes the AST and a
`errors: &mut Vec<CompileError>` sink, and emits
`CompileError::ConflictingTermType` directly when merging two concrete
types with different TypeIds.

Added `Signature::type_name(&Ast, TypeId) -> String` for formatting the
`types` field on the error. Morphism companions render as `Mor<...>`.

Locations are still a placeholder (`Location(0, 0)`) with a TODO
explaining that the self-hosted pass emits one error per source term
that resolves to the conflicting class, which needs per-element
provenance tracking on Structure.

build_structures returns (Structures, Vec<CompileError>); build.rs
destructures both but doesn't yet fold the errors into the main
stream (same TODO reason).
